=== exp2: AG+GEMM overlap granularity sweep ===
world 4, GEMM on GPU 0, pull mode, single serial comm stream
GPU 0: NVIDIA H20  sm_90  78 SMs  1980 MHz
GPU 1: NVIDIA H20  sm_90  78 SMs  1980 MHz
GPU 2: NVIDIA H20  sm_90  78 SMs  1980 MHz
GPU 3: NVIDIA H20  sm_90  78 SMs  1980 MHz

--- 8192x8192x8192 fp16 (shard M=2048, AG volume 96.0 MiB): full GEMM 7887.7 us, 139.4 TFLOP/s ---
   S   rows  chunkMiB |  t_seg us  segeff |    t_comm    GB/s |  t_ovl us  TFLOPs  ovl_eff   bub% | ver
   1   2048     32.00 |    8173.1   0.965 |     289.2   348.1 |    8205.0   134.0    0.889   0.4% | -
   2   1024     16.00 |    9358.0   0.843 |     314.1   320.5 |    9390.9   117.1    0.895   0.4% | -
   4    512      8.00 |    9405.7   0.839 |     368.5   273.1 |    9446.0   116.4    0.891   0.4% | -
   8    256      4.00 |    9529.2   0.828 |     466.5   215.8 |    9563.7   115.0    0.926   0.4% | -
  16    128      2.00 |   19002.3   0.415 |     719.5   139.9 |   19086.0    57.6    0.884   0.4% | -
  32     64      1.00 |   37983.4   0.208 |    1287.5    78.2 |   38116.5    28.8    0.897   0.4% | -

seg_eff = t_full/t_seg (segmentation-only GEMM efficiency).
ovl_eff = (t_seg + t_comm - t_ovl) / min(t_seg, t_comm); 1.0 means the
shorter phase is fully hidden. bub% = t_ovl over max(t_seg, t_comm).
The sweet spot is the S with the lowest t_ovl: finer chunks start compute
earlier but pay tile quantization + per-chunk signalling; coarser chunks
expose the first chunk's flight time.
